# Coordinated conditions: literals, states and objects
# with a preposition inside the condition. The canonical English form must reparse into the same IR.
While the module "m" prints "a" and "b", the module "m" uses the module "n".
If the state machine "sm" has the states "x" and "y", the module "m" starts the process "p".
The state machine "sm" starts in the state "x".
If the module "m" writes the record "r" and the record "s" to the file "f", the module "n" reads the file "f".
If the module "m" sends the message "a", the message "b" and the message "c" to the process "p" through the connection "k", the process "p" closes the connection "k".
When the module "m" reads the value "rate" and the value "z", the module "m" never changes the value "z".
